[1] Burnside obstruction at the first failure
For U(6), the nonzero symmetry types include fixed-point-free [3,3].
  cycle_type=[5, 1] class_size=144 fixed_tournaments=8 fixed_vertices=1
  cycle_type=[3, 3] class_size=40 fixed_tournaments=32 fixed_vertices=0
  cycle_type=[3, 1, 1, 1] class_size=40 fixed_tournaments=128 fixed_vertices=3
  cycle_type=[1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1] class_size=1 fixed_tournaments=32768 fixed_vertices=6
readout: rooted perspectives only see symmetries with a named vertex; the [3,3] term is a rootless cyclic sidecar, so depth on nodes alone cannot supply the eight missing U(6) classes.

